VOICE_STEPS_ANDROID=Hangul Learn! reads words and readings aloud with this device’s text-to-speech, which has no Korean voice yet. To add one:\n\n1. Tap Open settings below: it opens Text-to-speech output.\n2. As the preferred engine, choose Speech Services by Google.\n3. Tap the gear next to it, then Install voice data › Korean, and download it.\n4. Come back to Hangul Learn!: the speaker buttons appear by themselves.
VOICE_STEPS_IOS=Hangul Learn! reads words and readings aloud with this device’s voices, and none of them speaks Korean yet. To add one, open Settings › Accessibility › Spoken Content › Voices › Korean and download a voice. Then come back to Hangul Learn!: the speaker buttons appear by themselves.
SPEECH_BETTER_VOICE=For a clearer voice, download a Korean one in Settings › Accessibility › Spoken Content › Voices.
EXAM_INTRO=Each character once, from memory: a letter from its romanization, a hanja from its meaning and its sound.
ALBUM_EMPTY=Nothing practised yet: open a letter (Characters, or the Hangul chart), then Practice, then Score.
