HANGUL_CHARACTERS=Characters
LICENCE_LECTURES=Lectures
CREDITS=Hangul’s stroke order drawn for Hangul Learn!; the hanja’s from KanjiVG (CC BY-SA 3.0). Words, their levels and their meanings in English, Spanish, French and Japanese from the National Institute of Korean Language’s Basic Korean Dictionary (국립국어원 한국어기초사전, CC BY-SA 2.0 KR); the hanja’s readings from Unihan and libhangul, their meanings from KANJIDIC2 (EDRDG); example sentences from Tatoeba (tatoeba.org, CC BY 2.0 FR). Handwriting and text recognition by Google ML Kit, which sends Google anonymous usage data while it is on. Every licence in full: Licences.
WELCOME=Welcome
WELCOME_SKIP=Skip
WELCOME_START=Start writing
WELCOME_1_TITLE=Welcome to Hangul Learn!
WELCOME_1=Write Korean by hand, the way it is written: Hangul Learn! shows every letter’s strokes in order, reads what you write and tells you how well it went. It works offline, and everything stays on this device.
WELCOME_PHONE=Hangul Learn! is designed for tablets. It works on phones too, with less room to write.
WELCOME_2_TITLE=Pencil or finger
WELCOME_2_TITLE_ANDROID=Stylus or finger
WELCOME_2=Write with the Apple Pencil — fingers then move the page — or, with the hand on the bar, with one finger, and move the page with two. Hangul Learn! switches by itself when the Pencil writes. The tools are on a bar you can drag anywhere; a double tap on its handle folds it away.
WELCOME_2_ANDROID=Write with a stylus — fingers then move the page — or, with the hand on the bar, with one finger, and move the page with two. Hangul Learn! switches by itself when the stylus writes. The tools are on a bar you can drag anywhere; a double tap on its handle folds it away.
WELCOME_3_TITLE=Read with the camera
WELCOME_3=Tap the camera on the bar, or press and hold the page for Text from photo, and point it at Korean text: a book, a sign, a menu. Hangul Learn! reads it live and boxes each line: Hold keeps them, Write puts them on the page as handwriting to trace, and Translate with Google shows them in your language. A photo works too.
WELCOME_4_TITLE=Copy, paste, check
WELCOME_4=Draw around writing with the lasso: copy it, Copy as text to use it in any app, Check what it says, or Save word. Press and hold the page to paste: Paste text writes text copied anywhere as handwriting, stroke by stroke.
WELCOME_5_TITLE=Translate
WELCOME_5=Lasso your writing and choose Translate with Google to read it in your language. In Vocabulary, Translate with Google goes the other way: type in your language and get it in Korean, with its words to save, practise or write. The translation models download once, then work offline.
WELCOME_6_TITLE=Learn
WELCOME_6=The menu at the top left has everything to study: the Hangul chart, the letters and syllables with their stroke order, and the hanja; words by level to read and listen to, practice, reviews and exams. Lectures has free lessons, and the PDFs, photos and pages you scan, to read and write on.
WELCOME_7_TITLE=Your progress
WELCOME_7=Statistics shows your streak, the days you wrote, your scores week by week, your exams and the characters that need more work; the Album keeps every character you practised, with each try. It all stays on this device: Settings › Your data makes a backup.
LECTURE_PHRASEBOOK=Korean phrasebook
LECTURE_PHRASEBOOK_ABOUT=Hangul, pronunciation, a little grammar, and the phrases a trip needs (greetings, numbers, time, getting around, eating, shopping), with their romanization. From Wikivoyage.

